[[The Eameses]], USA, 1950.

A chair that changed its mind:

* It started in fiberglass
* Production stopped when fiberglass became an environmental worry
* It came back in 2004 in recyclable polypropylene
* Since 2022 the shell is made from 100% post-industrial recycled plastic

Same shape the whole time.

Compare the [[Navy Chair]], which also kept its form and swapped its material.
